From 6755cbb73aacda88b86e57b521e53b4daa22bef8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:12:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] services: handle frd/ptm calls, answer GetProcessInfo,
 quieter FS log

- frd:u / frd:a UpdateGameModeDescription (0x001D) and
  SetNotificationMask (0x0021): accept the request and return success.
  There is no friend server, so there's nothing to update or filter.
  Previously logged as unimplemented (Animal Crossing, 3DS Sound).
- ptm:* RegisterAlarmClient (0x0001): accept the event and return
  success; RTC alarms aren't emulated, so it is never signalled.
  Called by a system module on every boot.
- svcGetProcessInfo types 1/3 (supervisor stacks + handle table size),
  4 (used handles), 5 (highest handles, reported as current), 6 and 8
  (always 0) and 7 (thread count) now return values instead of leaving
  the output unset. Adds HandleTable::GetUsedCount with a test.
- "Delay generator was not initialized" is a normal fallback: log at
  debug level instead of error (it appeared on nearly every file open),
  and fix the "initalized" typo.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
